1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,913
Your boss arrives, and she has the right ships.

2
00:00:04,813 --> 00:00:09,161
But all she asks of the crew is, destroy everything,

3
00:00:09,611 --> 00:00:12,220
and she says nothing at all.

4
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:18,802
Today she gets objectives of her own, a way to lose,

5
00:00:19,252 --> 00:00:22,730
and a third ship she's been holding back.

6
00:00:23,630 --> 00:00:27,109
Most of it is lines you already know,

7
00:00:27,559 --> 00:00:30,602
and one small part is a card.

8
00:00:31,802 --> 00:00:34,411
First, read how a Siege ends,

9
00:00:34,861 --> 00:00:37,470
because your objectives hang on it.

10
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:41,413
There are four quests in this file.

11
00:00:42,313 --> 00:00:46,226
The top one wins the game when it's finished.

12
00:00:46,676 --> 00:00:51,459
Under it is Break the Siege, which wants every raider gone,

13
00:00:51,909 --> 00:00:54,952
and two more that lose the game.

14
00:00:56,752 --> 00:00:59,361
Now look at your own objective.

15
00:01:00,261 --> 00:01:03,739
It says its parent is that top quest.

16
00:01:04,639 --> 00:01:06,813
So with Required on it,

17
00:01:07,263 --> 00:01:12,915
it's one more thing the crew has to finish before they can win.

18
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:15,974
And without Required, it's a bonus.

19
00:01:17,174 --> 00:01:20,217
My objective is called Sink the Morrigan,

20
00:01:20,667 --> 00:01:24,146
but it's finished when every raider is gone.

21
00:01:25,046 --> 00:01:26,785
Let's make it honest.

22
00:01:27,685 --> 00:01:29,859
Done when, destroy one morrigan.

23
00:01:31,659 --> 00:01:34,267
That last word is a role,

24
00:01:34,717 --> 00:01:41,674
and the Siege gives every named ship its own name as a role, in small letters.

25
00:01:42,574 --> 00:01:46,052
So whatever you wrote on the Named line

26
00:01:46,502 --> 00:01:49,546
is a word you can use here.

27
00:01:50,746 --> 00:01:53,789
A second objective, for her second ship.

28
00:01:54,689 --> 00:01:56,863
It has no Required line,

29
00:01:57,313 --> 00:02:03,400
so it pays if they do it and it doesn't matter if they don't.

30
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:07,374
After that comes a clock.

31
00:02:08,274 --> 00:02:12,187
Fails when, thirty seconds, which is a test number.

32
00:02:12,637 --> 00:02:14,811
Then Fatal, set to true,

33
00:02:15,261 --> 00:02:20,913
and a Lose line, with the sentence the crew reads when it's over.

34
00:02:21,813 --> 00:02:23,552
Use those three together.

35
00:02:24,452 --> 00:02:28,800
And then I play it and I don't touch anything,

36
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:35,337
and half a minute after she arrives, the game is lost, in my words.

37
00:02:36,237 --> 00:02:39,715
Then I set the real limit, ten minutes,

38
00:02:40,165 --> 00:02:43,209
and I say so in the objective,

39
00:02:43,659 --> 00:02:48,876
because the game doesn't warn the crew as the time runs down.

40
00:02:50,076 --> 00:02:54,424
Some things no line in a boss file can say,

41
00:02:54,874 --> 00:02:59,657
and a ship that turns up later is one of them.

42
00:03:00,557 --> 00:03:04,904
For those, a boss has one more line, called Hook.

43
00:03:05,804 --> 00:03:08,413
It names a block of script,

44
00:03:08,863 --> 00:03:13,211
and the Siege runs that block once, when she arrives.

45
00:03:15,011 --> 00:03:18,924
One hook comes with the game, so try it.

46
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:25,041
And there's a swarm of BioMechs, with no script written by me.

47
00:03:25,941 --> 00:03:28,115
They aren't her story, though.

48
00:03:28,565 --> 00:03:31,174
So now we write her own.

49
00:03:32,374 --> 00:03:36,287
This is the one awkward thing in the lecture.

50
00:03:37,187 --> 00:03:42,839
Your boss file lives in common data, where an update never touches it.

51
00:03:43,739 --> 00:03:45,913
But a hook is script,

52
00:03:46,363 --> 00:03:50,711
and script has to be inside the Legendary Missions folder.

53
00:03:52,511 --> 00:03:56,859
So I make a folder of my own in there,

54
00:03:57,309 --> 00:03:59,483
with one file in it,

55
00:03:59,933 --> 00:04:05,150
named with two underscores, the word init, two more underscores, dot mast.

56
00:04:06,050 --> 00:04:10,398
I haven't changed any file that came with the game.

57
00:04:11,298 --> 00:04:15,211
But an update replaces that whole folder, mine included,

58
00:04:15,661 --> 00:04:19,139
so keep a copy of it somewhere else.

59
00:04:20,339 --> 00:04:22,948
Here's the smallest hook there is.

60
00:04:23,848 --> 00:04:28,196
A label, which is three equals signs and a name.

61
00:04:28,646 --> 00:04:32,993
One line that says a sentence to every crew ship.

62
00:04:33,443 --> 00:04:36,052
And the line that ends it.

63
00:04:36,952 --> 00:04:41,300
Then the boss file names that label, letter for letter.

64
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:48,317
Now there are two things to check, so there are two commands.

65
00:04:49,217 --> 00:04:52,696
The first reads my boss file, as always.

66
00:04:53,596 --> 00:04:57,943
The second reads all of Legendary Missions, my card included,

67
00:04:58,393 --> 00:05:00,567
the way the game will.

68
00:05:01,467 --> 00:05:03,207
Read its last line.

69
00:05:03,657 --> 00:05:05,396
You want zero errors.

70
00:05:06,296 --> 00:05:11,078
The two warnings are in files that came with the game,

71
00:05:11,528 --> 00:05:15,441
so they're not yours and you leave them alone.

72
00:05:16,641 --> 00:05:19,685
Now the card grows by four lines.

73
00:05:20,585 --> 00:05:25,367
A wait, which is one of your cards from Class 1.

74
00:05:25,817 --> 00:05:29,730
A line that stops if the game's already over.

75
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:34,093
One long line that brings in a named ship.

76
00:05:34,543 --> 00:05:38,891
And your finish a step card, which sends a signal.

77
00:05:40,691 --> 00:05:45,474
On the ship line you change four things and nothing else:

78
00:05:45,924 --> 00:05:49,837
where she appears, her name, which ship she is,

79
00:05:50,287 --> 00:05:55,070
and her name again in small letters, which is her role.

80
00:05:56,270 --> 00:06:01,052
A signal finishes a step, and a step can reveal another.

81
00:06:01,502 --> 00:06:04,111
That's the chain from Class 1.

82
00:06:05,011 --> 00:06:08,054
So Her Reserve waits for the signal,

83
00:06:08,504 --> 00:06:12,417
and when it's done it reveals Sink the Nemain.

84
00:06:14,217 --> 00:06:16,391
Two things here catch people.

85
00:06:17,291 --> 00:06:23,813
In a boss file, the address after reveal is the key alone, with no slash.

86
00:06:24,713 --> 00:06:28,191
And the hidden step says, starts when revealed,

87
00:06:28,641 --> 00:06:31,685
and does not also say, state active.

88
00:06:32,885 --> 00:06:35,059
Run both of them again.

89
00:06:35,959 --> 00:06:40,741
And look at what a mistake in the card costs you.

90
00:06:41,641 --> 00:06:44,250
I'll take out one quote mark.

91
00:06:45,150 --> 00:06:49,063
Lint gives me an error that ends, mast compile,

92
00:06:49,513 --> 00:06:52,122
with the file and the line.

93
00:06:53,922 --> 00:06:58,270
If I played that, nothing in Legendary Missions would run.

94
00:06:58,720 --> 00:07:01,763
No Siege, and no other map either.

95
00:07:02,663 --> 00:07:06,576
Your Class 1 cards were in your own mission.

96
00:07:07,026 --> 00:07:09,200
This one's inside the game's,

97
00:07:09,650 --> 00:07:13,998
so run that second command every time you touch it.

98
00:07:15,198 --> 00:07:18,241
And now she arrives and says so.

99
00:07:19,141 --> 00:07:22,185
Three objectives are in the Quest Log,

100
00:07:22,635 --> 00:07:25,243
and the fourth isn't there yet.

101
00:07:26,143 --> 00:07:28,752
Ten seconds later, there's the Nemain,

102
00:07:29,202 --> 00:07:33,115
Her Reserve is done, and the fourth one appears.

103
00:07:34,915 --> 00:07:37,524
Then put the real numbers back:

104
00:07:37,974 --> 00:07:39,713
forty percent, ten minutes,

105
00:07:40,163 --> 00:07:42,772
and ninety seconds on the card.

106
00:07:43,972 --> 00:07:47,885
Your boss is now two things in two places.

107
00:07:48,785 --> 00:07:51,828
The file is safe from an update,

108
00:07:52,278 --> 00:07:54,017
and the folder isn't.

109
00:07:54,917 --> 00:07:58,396
After an update she's still in the list,

110
00:07:58,846 --> 00:08:01,454
and she arrives without her hook:

111
00:08:01,904 --> 00:08:04,513
no sentence, and no reserve ship.

112
00:08:06,313 --> 00:08:08,052
Lint tells you, too.

113
00:08:08,502 --> 00:08:13,720
It warns that Her Reserve is waiting for a signal nothing sends.

114
00:08:14,620 --> 00:08:17,663
So keep a copy of that folder,

115
00:08:18,113 --> 00:08:21,157
and put it back after every update.

116
00:08:22,057 --> 00:08:25,970
Next time is the last lecture of the class,

117
00:08:26,420 --> 00:08:28,593
and she gets a voice.
